  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>The process of conversion of primary aromatic amines into its&nbsp;diazonium&nbsp;salt is called&nbsp;diazotization.&nbsp;</p><p>Diazonium&nbsp;salts are important synthetic intermediates that can undergo coupling&nbsp;reactions&nbsp;to form azo dyes and electrophilic substitution&nbsp;reactions&nbsp;to introduce functional groups.</p><p>The&nbsp;correct sequence of reagents used for converting nitrobenzene into m- dibromobenzene is found in option (b).</p><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/aefa6f34-12ff-4a77-af80-87730cc54f35-image.png\" style=\"width: 373px; height: 353px;\" /></p>",
